First, some background. When the website is wide, the sidebars are displayed directly on the page as sidebars. When the website is narrow, some CSS kicks in to make the sidebars into invisible drawers, or overlays, that become visible when the user clicks a button. A nice feature of the way this was implemented is that both the sidebars and the drawers share the same exact HTML. In other words, the HTML is not duplicated on the page so that you have one HTML tree for the sidebar and another HTML tree for the drawer.

For the mobile presentation of the sidebar content, I want to use the native HTML dialog element because it comes with all of the modal functionality that we want built in, which means less JavaScript code to write and maintain on our end. However, it would be incorrect to use the dialog element for the desktop presentation of the same content because it is not in a dialog, which is a descendant window of the primary window—it is in a sidebar.

That means that we have to have two different root nodes for the sidebar:

- Mobile: `<dialog>`
- Desktop: `<div>`

One possible solution would be to render the Jinja templates twice, once in the dialog element and once in the div. However, this increases the byte size of the HTML page and it creates potential HTML element id conflicts. 

So that's why I chose this implementation in which I move the sidebar content nodes from the div to the dialog, when the user clicks the button to open the mobile dialog, and then move them back when the user closes the mobile dialog.","created_at":"2024-08-08T16:55:23Z","updated_at":"2024-08-08T16:55:23Z","html_url":"https://github.com/pydata/pydata-sphinx-theme/pull/1942#discussion_r1709920998","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pydata/pydata-sphinx-theme/pulls/1942","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/pydata/pydata-sphinx-theme/pulls/comments/1709920998"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/pydata/pydata-sphinx-theme/pull/1942#discussion_r1709920998"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/pydata/pydata-sphinx-theme/pulls/1942"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pydata/pydata-sphinx-theme/pulls/comments/1709920998/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":718,"original_line":718,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":1697206272,"original_position":155,"position":155,"subject_type":"line"},"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pydata/pydata-sphinx-theme/pulls/1942","id":1994718976,"node_id":"PR_kwDOB8NEQs525P8A","html_url":"https://github.com/pydata/pydata-sphinx-theme/pull/1942","diff_url":"https://github.com/pydata/pydata-sphinx-theme/pull/1942.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/pydata/pydata-sphinx-theme/pull/1942.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pydata/pydata-sphinx-theme/issues/1942","number":1942,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Make overlay sidebars behave like modals","user":{"login":"gabalafou","id":317883,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxNzg4Mw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/317883?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gabalafou","html_url":"https://github.com